        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Friedrich Hayek, William Warren Bartley\n- Products: The Fatal Conceit\n- Topics: Socialism, classical liberalism\n\nFacts:\n- Friedrich Hayek was born on 8 May 1899 in Austria-Hungary as Friedrich August von Hayek.\n- The Fatal Conceit: The Errors of Socialism is a 1988 non-fiction book written by Friedrich Hayek and edited by William Warren Bartley.\n- Friedrich Hayek was an Austrian-British economist and philosopher.\n- Friedrich Hayek was frequently referred to as F. A. Hayek.\n- Friedrich Hayek is best known for his defense of classical liberalism.",
